{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Plan review PASSED (verdict PASS, 0 blocking, 2 advisory) at head_sha ee2c54f881d6, signed.\n\nAdvisory f2af906e (COH/E6, triage bucket apply-now) — 'does a raw pytest.importorskip satisfy AC4, or must the fix call a tests/_extra_guard.py helper?'. APPLIED, and the reconciliation is: the raw call IS the sanctioned call. tests/_extra_guard.py exposes no per-test helper API; conftest.py calls _extra_guard.install(), which REBINDS pytest.importorskip itself to strict_importorskip when REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1. So one identical call site gets both sides. Empirically confirmed in this worktree:\n  - extra absent, no env var  -> 15 passed, 1 skipped (SKIPPED ... could not import 'hcl2')\n  - extra absent, REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1 -> 1 failed, 15 passed, raised from tests/_extra_guard.py:58 as ImportError, NOT a skip\n  - extra installed (python-hcl2==8.1.3) -> 16 passed\n  - extra installed + REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1 (the true gating-lane config) -> 16 passed\nThe guard's comment in the test now states this explicitly so the next reader does not re-raise the same question.\n\nAdvisory f607dd45 (P6 ac-quality, triage bucket defer, priority 0.40 vs a 0.95 block line) — one AC line bundles two deliverables with 'and' (AC1: guard present AND the other 15 still run). DEFERRED. Rewording the description would change the plan material and invalidate the signed attestation on a bug that is currently reddening main; the substance is verified anyway, both halves demonstrated separately by the runs above. No behavioural gap."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788547792721471001,"uuid":"8fb81f29-9d27-4e70-8218-317ace860693"}